# Diagnosis — V2i drives time out on real Claude in Docker

- date: 2026-09-27
- branch: fix/cli-254-v2i-theme-picker-seed
- diagnosed_via: Path C probe (5 turns) + PR #269 characterization run

## Step 0 — Reproduce
- Command: docker-smoke workflow run against v1.9.4 (baseline)
- Observed: 3 interactive drives (/onboard-repo, /launch, /riff) exit 11
  which maps to exit 31 (EXIT_INTERACTIVE_TIMEOUT) via entry.sh V2i wrapper.
- Log source: harness-out/interactive-2026-09-27T14-03-59Z/interactive/drive.log
- Reproducibility: every drive, every V2i run.

## Step 1 — Is / Is Not
- IS: Real Claude in Docker, freshly launched, first-run.
- IS NOT: fake_claude.sh fixture (drives PASS against fixture per PR #260).
- IS NOT: `claude -p` non-interactive mode (skips first-run onboarding).
- Similar thing that WORKS: `claude -p "hello"` in the same container.

## Step 2 — Five Whys
1. Why do drives exit 11? expect timeout waits 90s for READY>; never appears.
2. Why does READY> never appear? Claude never reaches REPL — blocks on prior UI.
3. What does Claude show instead? "Welcome to Claude Code v2.1.197" then
   "Choose a theme" picker (options 1-7).
4. Why the picker? First-run of claude with no ~/.claude/settings.json (or
   missing theme field) triggers it.
5. Why fresh every run? Docker image builds a clean adopter home; no state
   carries the theme choice forward.

## Step 3 — Hypothesis
Pre-seeding /home/adopter/.claude/settings.json with {"theme": "dark"} at
Docker build time lets Claude skip the theme picker and drop straight to a
REPL prompt.

## Falsifiable test
Build modified image; run V2i with SMOKE_GH_TOKEN set; read drive.log. If
the log shows a REPL prompt within 90s, hypothesis is confirmed. If a
second gate appears, hypothesis is partly confirmed and a second field
is needed.

## Alternative explanations (Peirce)
- Alt-A: Auth failure — ruled out; `claude -p` works with same token.
- Alt-B: TTY missing — ruled out; expect provides a pty; Claude renders
  the picker UI (which needs a tty).
- Alt-C: Theme picker plus a second gate. Possible. Falsification path:
  read drive.log after seed lands; if second gate appears, extend
  settings.json in a follow-on.
